  "subject": "a young man in Depok who rides every month with his girlfriend to the vet for her old one-eyed cat, steering the motorbike while she sits behind holding the blue carrier on her lap, and realizes this is the part of the week he waits for",
  "caption": "Indonesian guitar-led male pop love ballad, 2020s streaming-era style. Fingerpicked nylon-string guitar with a second steel-string guitar strumming softly in the chorus, gentle sustained piano chords, round warm bass, light brushed drums entering at the first chorus. Clean intimate mix, close-miked, natural room. Tender male tenor vocal, clear diction, soft falsetto touches on chorus peaks. 74 BPM, D major. Mood of quiet devoted love on an ordinary errand. No dramatic orchestra swell, no trap beat, no autotune, no electric guitar solo, no gospel choir.",
  "lyrics": "[Intro - nylon guitar, soft piano]\n[Verse 1]\nSabtu pagi kau sudah siap\nKandang biru di pangkuanmu\nSi Item mengeong satu mata\nKau bilang, \"Pelan-pelan, ya, Sayang\"\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAku pegang setang motor\nKau pegang kandang dan pinggangku\n[Chorus]\nJalan ke dokter hewan\nLima belas menit saja\nTapi aku ingin lampu merah\nLebih lama di tiap simpang\n[Verse 2]\nDi ruang tunggu kau berbisik\nKe kucing tua yang ketakutan\nAku pura-pura baca brosur\nPadahal aku menatapmu terus\n[Chorus]\nJalan ke dokter hewan\nLima belas menit saja\nTapi aku sudah hafal\nHangat tanganmu di pinggangku\n[Bridge - piano alone, then guitar returns]\nKalau suatu hari kita menua\nBiar aku tetap yang di depan\n[Outro - soft guitar fade]\nKandang biru di jok belakang\nKau dan aku, pulang pelan-pelan",
